# Testing rules

- Financial/security bugs always receive regression tests.
- Unit tests cover pure domain logic; integration tests use real PostgreSQL for transactions/constraints/concurrency.
- Default test/CI must not use production DB, production credentials or spend real AI/payment money.
- Test duplicate/replay/concurrent cases, not only happy paths.
- Auth tests include unauthorized access, ownership/IDOR, session invalidation, enumeration-safe responses and OTP/recovery abuse when implemented.
- AI tests include no-usage-no-provider-call, duplicate request, malformed stream, missing usage, disconnect/ambiguous outcome, rate/concurrency limits and secret redaction.
- Admin tests include default deny, permission boundaries, MFA/step-up policy hooks, production route isolation and audit events.
- i18n tests should detect missing required RU/EN keys for critical flows.
- Quality gate: lint + typecheck + tests + integration tests + build before phase completion.
